


--> Spring JDBC & JdbcTemplate
    Role of JDBC in Spring Applications
    JDBC (Java Database Connectivity) is the core API that allows Java applications to connect and interact with databases using SQL.
    In Spring-based applications:
            JDBC is used internally
            Spring provides higher-level abstractions to simplify JDBC usage
    Spring JDBC sits on top of JDBC and removes boilerplate code.

--> Problems with Traditional JDBC
        Traditional JDBC requires:
        Manual connection creation
        Manual closing of resources
        Repeated try-catch blocks
        Error-prone code
        Example issues:
            Forgetting to close ResultSet
            SQLExceptions everywhere
            Too much repetitive code

--> How Spring JDBC Solves These Problems
        Spring JDBC provides:
        Automatic resource management
        Simplified exception handling
        Cleaner code using JdbcTemplate
        ✅ No need to:
        Open/close connections
        Write repetitive try-catch-finally blocks

--> Configure DataSource (application.properties)
    Spring Boot auto-configures the DataSource when DB properties are provided.

    spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/testdb
    spring.datasource.username=root
    spring.datasource.password=admin
    spring.datasource.driver-class-name=com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver

    Spring Boot automatically creates:
        DataSource
        JdbcTemplate bean



--> Statement vs PreparedStatement vs JdbcTemplate

    | Feature        | Statement | PreparedStatement | JdbcTemplate |
    | -------------- | --------- | ----------------- | ------------ |
    | SQL Injection  | ❌ Unsafe  | ✅ Safe            | ✅ Safe       |
    | Boilerplate    | ❌ High    | ❌ Medium          | ✅ Very Low   |
    | Performance    | ❌ Poor    | ✅ Better          | ✅ Optimized  |
    | Spring Support | ❌ No      | ❌ Limited         | ✅ Full       |

